WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.640
Before we take any action, we need to talk about universal precautions.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.060
These are the steps you take to keep yourself safe while you are helping someone else.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:13.040
The most important rule in first aid is to protect yourself first.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:18.480
You should always assume that all blood and bodily fluids, like saliva or vomit, are infectious,

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.200
so you must handle them with extreme care.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.440
Using personal protective equipment, or PPE, is ideal.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.360
If PPE isn't available in an emergency, you'll need to use your best judgment to provide

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.759
care as safely as you can.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:37.500
We highly recommend wearing non-latex gloves whenever you are providing any kind of aid

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.200
to an injured person.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.840
If you are worried about splashes of blood or vomit, use eye protection and a mask to

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.360
keep you safe.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:50.580
Once you are finished, make sure to dispose of all your used PPE properly so no one else

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.299
comes into contact with it.

00:00:52.299 --> 00:00:57.599
If you do happen to get exposed to someone else's blood or body fluids, don't panic.

00:00:57.599 --> 00:01:01.119
Your first step is to immediately wash the area with soap and water.

00:01:01.119 --> 00:01:05.959
If you suspect there was any cross-contamination or a significant exposure, be sure to report

00:01:05.959 --> 00:01:08.360
the incident to your healthcare provider right away.

